{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg73k5rkJY7JQmb1YEZ39","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Firecrawl caches scrapes by default, and the `maxAge` parameter controls how old a cached copy can be.\n\n**Default:** In the v2 API, `maxAge` defaults to 2 days (172,800,000 ms). If an identical scrape was cached within that window, you get the cached copy. This is why pages look stale.\n\n**Force a fresh scrape:** Set `maxAge` to `0`.\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.firecrawl.dev/v2/scrape \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $FIRECRAWL_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"url\": \"https://example.com\", \"maxAge\": 0}'\n```\n\n```python\napp.scrape(\"https://example.com\", max_age=0)   # Python SDK\n```\n\n```js\nawait firecrawl.scrape(\"https://example.com\", { maxAge: 0 });  // JS SDK\n```\n\n**Related options:**\n- `maxAge` is in milliseconds. For example, `3600000` accepts a cached copy up to 1 hour old. That is a good middle ground if you don't need real-time data on every call, because cache hits are much faster.\n- `storeInCache: false` stops that scrape from being written to the cache. This is useful for sensitive or one-off pages. It doesn't bypass reads, so pair it with `maxAge: 0` for a fully uncached scrape.\n- Crawl, batch scrape, and search accept the same scrape options (nested under `scrapeOptions` for crawl and search), so set `maxAge: 0` there too if those are the calls returning stale data.\n\n**If it's still stale with `maxAge: 0`:**\n- The origin site's own CDN or server cache may be serving the old version. Firecrawl can't bypass that.\n- The content may load via JavaScript after the initial render. Add a `waitFor` delay (ms) or use actions to wait for it.\n- If you call the API through a wrapper, MCP server, or your own cache layer, check that it passes `maxAge` through.\n\nI'm going from memory on the 2-day default, which could change. The scrape docs at docs.firecrawl.dev list the current value. I can look it up if you'd like."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6869,"cache_read_input_tokens":11227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6869},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e5f998b-6371-4e74-8af7-260b4436e864","uuid":"5daa7b5e-a9d5-4d2f-b327-2f6702f131a6","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:49:31.814Z","request_id":"req_011Cg73k5f6o2DKxyUi6kKP3"}
